---
description: Mixed-document rule (critical) — invoice plus attachments is still an invoice
alwaysApply: true
---

Many files are an invoice PLUS attachments.

If ANY page is a true invoice or credit note, classify from that commercial document.
Ignore later supporting pages when choosing the label.

Examples that MUST be INVOICE (not BOL / PACKING_LIST / TERMS / OTHER):
- Page 1 is an invoice, page 2 is a Bill of Lading.
- Invoice followed by packing list, delivery receipt, POD, or shipping papers.
- Invoice followed by terms & conditions, warranty, or legal pages.
- Invoice followed by rate confirmation, load confirmation, or carrier paperwork.

Do NOT switch the label to BOL, PACKING_LIST, or TERMS just because those words appear on page 2 or later.
Only use BOL / PACKING_LIST / TERMS when there is NO invoice and NO credit note in the OCR text.
